{"step_index":692,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-07T03:30:19Z","thinking":"Examining the user's question about free alternatives to the Supreme Court Registry for verifying corporate registration numbers. Investigating potential avenues within the Korean public administration and business information systems to identify possible free, legal methods for obtaining this information. The objective is to compile a complete list of all legitimate, free alternatives.\n\n\nInvestigating potential free resources for verifying corporate registration numbers in South Korea. First, considering the 국세청 홈택스 (Hometax), specifically the e-invoice issuance/inquiry section. If the business is a trading partner, business registration information may be available, although the corporation number is not always required on invoices.\n\nConsidering the 공정거래위원회 통신판매사업자 조회, where all businesses that report themselves as 通信판매 are required to make their 법인등록번호 public. Then, checking 고용노동부 워크넷/고용24 for companies that posted job openings, as it sometimes includes the corporation number. Finally, exploring K-report, Cretop, and SMINFO as potential information sources.\n\n\nInvestigating the 중소기업현황정보시스템 for businesses with 중소기업 확인서, as their information might be accessible. Also, KED (한국평가데이터) is another potential source.\n\nChecking 정부24 (Gov24), 세움터, and 나라장터, specifically 나라장터, since businesses registered for bidding might have publicly available 法人등록번호.\n\nThen, investigating the 대법원 인터넷등기소. Even without paying for 등기부등본 열람, the 무료 상호 검색 might reveal partial 法人등록번호 and status. Checking other 무료 메뉴 for possible 法人등록번호 disclosure. Considering direct contact with the company as a definitive, free method.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"site:work.go.kr \"바른중량\" OR \"7758100670\"","toolAction":"Searching worknet for 바른중량","toolSummary":"Search worknet 바른중량"}}]}
